---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Edoardo Rossi — marketing as the meeting point between business and psychology: understanding people through data, and data through people."
  translated
>
  <section class="about container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Marketing is where business meets psychology.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      That's what brought me here, and it's what keeps me here. Behind every metric is a
      behavior; behind every behavior, a person making a decision. The anthropological side of
      the job — understanding who you're talking to, what they're really looking for, why they
      choose — interests me as much as the analytical one. If anything, I believe one doesn't
      work without the other.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data, on its own, tells you what happened. People, on their own, tell stories that the
      numbers sometimes contradict. My work sits in between: using analysis to give clear answers
      on who, what and why — and using those answers to build campaigns, funnels and positioning
      that treat the audience as people, not segments.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm someone who always looks for the extra step: understanding the process beyond the
      campaign, the business beyond the brief, the outcome beyond the report. In my
      <a href={`${base}en/work/`}>case studies</a> you'll find how this approach plays out in
      practice — real numbers, stated limitations included.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: var(--space-6); max-width: 46rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; }
</style>
